From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 18:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: cix: mvx: set the vb2 queue lock to the session mutex

setup_vb2_queue() does not set vb2_queue.lock. Point it at the session
mutex so that the vb2 ioctl helpers and file operations are serialised with
the driver's own session locking.

Tested on an Orange Pi 6 Plus (CIX CD8180) with 6.18.14 and the Sky1
series, together with the previous patch: a 2h44 HEVC encode with
hevc_v4l2m2m completes at the same speed (about 313 fps) with no vb2
warning in dmesg.

Signed-off-by: kennytech73 <contact@bookworm-mon0.org>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c
@@ -706,6 +706,7 @@ static int setup_vb2_queue(struct mvx_v4l2_port *vport)
     q->ops = &mvx_vb2_ops;
     q->mem_ops = &vb2_dma_sg_memops;
     q->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_COPY;
+    q->lock = &vport->vsession->mutex;
     q->allow_zero_bytesused = true;
     if (vport->dir == MVX_DIR_OUTPUT && mvx_is_frame(vport->port->format))
         q->MVX_VB2_MIN_BUFFERS_NEEDED = 8;
